Failure of Calderón-Zygmund estimates for degenerate elliptic PDEs with 𝐴_𝑝-weights when 𝑝>2 Skip to main content Report GitHub Issue × Title: Content selection saved. Describe the issue below: Description: Why HTML? Report Issue Back to Abstract Download PDF Contents Reading mode Colour theme License: arXiv.org perpetual non-exclusive license arXiv:2605.15414v1 [math.AP] 14 May 2026 Failure of Calderón-Zygmund estimates for degenerate elliptic PDEs with A p A_{p} -weights when p > 2 p>2 Armin Schikorra Armin Schikorra Department of Mathematics, University of Pittsburgh, 301 Thackeray Hall, Pittsburgh, PA 15260, USA and Department of Mathematics, Chulalongkorn University, Bangkok, Thailand Email address: armin@pitt.edu and Martin Ulmer Martin Ulmer Department of Mathematics, Brown University, 151 Thayer Street, Providence, RI 02912, USA Email address: martin_ulmer@brown.edu Abstract. We use convex integration techniques to provide examples of failure of weighted Calderón-Zygmund estimates for degenerate linear elliptic PDEs when the weights are in A p A_{p} , p > 2 p>2 . 1. Introduction We consider solutions u u to linear degenerate elliptic PDEs of the form div ( w ∇ u ) = div ( w F ) {m div}(w
abla u)={m div}(wF) with a Muckenhoupt weight w w , and are interested in the classical Calderón-Zygmund theory. The purpose of this work is to investigate whether Calderón–Zygmund-type estimates persist for degenerate elliptic equations beyond the natural class of A 2 A_{2} weights, and we show that this is not the case. We work on the simple domain 𝔹 n \mathbb{B}^{n} , the unit ball in dimension n n . Let A r = A r ​ ( μ ) A_{r}=A_{r}(\mu) be the Muckenhoupt class with respect to the Lebesgue measure, and we denote by w : ℝ n → ( 0 , ∞ ) w:\mathbb{R}^{n}	o(0,\infty) a weight with characteristic [ w ] A r := sup Q ( ∫ Q ⁡ w ) ​ ( ∫ Q ⁡ w − 1 r − 1 ) r − 1 [w]_{A_{r}}:=\sup_{Q}\left(\mathchoice{\mathop{\vrule width=6.0pt,height=3.0pt,depth=-2.5pt\kern-8.0pt\intop}
